Session identifiers can be regenerated after authentication to mitigate fixation risks.
Session expiration limits session lifetime.
Logging out should invalidate or otherwise terminate authenticated session authority according to application design.
Deleting a visible client cookie alone may not invalidate server-side session state.
HttpOnly prevents ordinary browser JavaScript from reading the cookie.
