A timeout should report the operation that timed out.
A timeout waiting for an upstream service is not the same as a malformed client request.
A timeout waiting for a local database is not automatically a gateway timeout.
System architecture determines the correct error classification.
Retries can also duplicate state-changing operations.
A client should not blindly retry every failed request.
Idempotent operations are generally safer to retry.
