When persistent state appears wrong, identify the authoritative source.
Identify recent writes.
Identify transaction results.
Identify storage errors.
Identify recovery events.
Identify backup state.
Do not overwrite evidence before understanding the failure.
Preserve the suspect state when practical.
Recovery and investigation can require different copies.
When an incident ends, verify restoration.
Verify required operations.
Verify dependency state.
Verify queues are recovering.
Verify error rate returned to expected range.
Verify latency returned to expected range.
