A version field can identify format version.
Versioning allows formats to evolve.
An unsupported version should be rejected clearly.
Do not silently interpret unknown versions as the newest known version.
Do not silently ignore required unknown semantics.
Forward compatibility should be designed, not assumed.
Backward compatibility means newer software can read or interact with older supported data according to defined rules.
Compatibility has scope.
A format can be backward compatible but not forward compatible.
