Negative tests are important.
Valid input is only part of an interface.
Invalid input should produce defined behavior.
Malformed input should not cause undefined behavior.
Missing input should be handled according to interface rules.
Oversized input should be bounded.
Testing should include boundaries.
One can be a boundary.
Maximum values can be boundaries.
Empty input can be a boundary.
Maximum permitted length can be a boundary.
