The same valid message under the same protocol version should have the same defined meaning.
Implementation-specific interpretation should not alter protocol semantics.
A request asks another participant to perform or provide something according to protocol semantics.
Not every protocol is request-response.
Some protocols are event-driven.
Some protocols use streaming.
Some protocols use publish-subscribe.
Some protocols combine these patterns.
