memcpy is commonly useful for moving object representation bytes without violating ordinary aliasing rules when used correctly.
Endianness describes byte ordering for multibyte values.
Little-endian stores the least significant byte at the lowest address.
Big-endian stores the most significant byte at the lowest address.
Native machine endianness should not be assumed in portable serialized formats.
Convert when reading.
Convert when writing.
Compiler intrinsics expose implementation-specific operations or processor features.
Intrinsics can provide efficient access to special instructions.
Intrinsics reduce portability.
Isolate architecture-specific optimization behind stable interfaces when portability matters.
Inline assembly is compiler and architecture specific.
Inline assembly should be used only when requirements justify it.
Modern compilers can generate highly optimized machine code.
Measure before replacing portable code with architecture-specific code.
Profile-guided optimization uses runtime profile information to guide compilation decisions.
Link-time optimization allows optimization across translation-unit boundaries during linking or an integrated link stage.
LTO can improve optimization opportunities.
LTO can increase build time.
