Use it when requirements and evidence justify it.
Whole-program optimization can expose relationships unavailable during separate compilation.
Separate compilation is valuable because one source file can be rebuilt without recompiling an entire project.
Header changes can cause many dependent translation units to rebuild.
Incorrect dependency tracking can create stale builds.
A stale object file can contain code from an older source state.
Clean builds help detect stale-artifact problems.
If behavior appears impossible according to current source, verify that the executable actually contains the current build.
Check timestamps where useful.
Check hashes where useful.
Do not debug source that is not actually running.
Out-of-tree builds can keep source trees clean.
Generated files should have defined ownership.
Do not manually edit generated artifacts when they will be overwritten by the build.
A build script records build commands.
A build script improves repeatability.
A build script should identify compiler options.
A build script should identify source files.
A build script should identify library paths.
A build script should identify linked libraries.
A build script should fail when required compilation fails.
A build script should not report success after a failed compiler command.
Exit status communicates command success or failure.
Continuing after a failed compilation can create misleading stale output.
Compiler command order matters.
Library order can matter for some static linkers.
Object and library dependencies should be expressed correctly.
Do not randomly reorder linker arguments until a build succeeds without understanding why.
Include paths tell the preprocessor where to search for headers.
Include paths and library paths are different.
A header being found does not prove the required library will be found.
Header and binary versions should be compatible.
Package development files commonly provide headers and link-time metadata.
Building and running have different dependency requirements.
A compiler can search default include directories.
Environment variables can modify toolchain search behavior.
Hidden environment configuration can make builds non-reproducible.
Prefer explicit build configuration where practical.
pkg-config can provide compiler and linker flags for installed libraries on systems using that mechanism.
Build systems can query dependency metadata.
Dependency discovery should fail clearly when required libraries are absent.
Do not silently disable required functionality because a dependency was not found unless the build policy explicitly permits it.
Optional dependencies should be clearly identified as optional.
Platform detection identifies the target environment.
Feature detection is often more precise than assuming every system of one name has identical capabilities.
Compiler predefined macros can identify implementation or target characteristics.
Do not scatter platform checks throughout common logic without need.
Centralize platform adaptation where architecture benefits from it.
A platform abstraction provides a common interface over platform-specific implementations.
The common interface defines required semantics.
Each backend implements those semantics for its platform.
Platform independence requires equivalent externally required behavior.
Platform independence does not require identical source code for every operating system.
Platform-specific implementation is compatible with platform-independent architecture when the differences remain behind controlled interfaces.
The compiler selects or builds the appropriate implementation according to build or runtime architecture.
Runtime platform selection chooses implementation while executing.
These approaches solve different requirements.
Compiler errors should be read from the first relevant diagnostic.
One syntax error can cause many later diagnostics.
Later errors can be consequences of an earlier parse failure.
Fix the earliest root diagnostic and rebuild.
Do not patch every cascading diagnostic independently.
Linker errors should be interpreted according to symbol resolution.
Undefined reference means a definition was not resolved.
