Hot loading requires a stable host-module contract.
The host should validate version compatibility.
The host should validate ABI expectations.
The host should reject incompatible modules.
A rejected module should not execute merely because it was discovered.
A module should not modify host behavior before qualification completes unless the architecture explicitly permits that behavior.
A module can expose a shutdown function.
A module can expose capability functions.
The compiler does not define the application module contract.
The application architecture defines it.
Build metadata can embed version information.
Build metadata can embed commit identifiers.
Build metadata can embed target architecture.
Build metadata can embed build timestamps.
