Do not confuse compilation with linking.
Do not confuse linking with loading.
Do not confuse loading with initialization.
Do not confuse a declaration with a definition.
Do not confuse language linkage with the linker.
Do not confuse API with ABI.
Do not confuse an import library with a DLL.
Do not confuse successful linking with runtime success.
Do not confuse debug behavior with release behavior.
Do not confuse compiler warnings with runtime errors.
Do not confuse implementation-defined behavior with undefined behavior.
Do not confuse unspecified behavior with undefined behavior.
Do not confuse compiler extensions with standard language features.
Do not confuse source order with generated instruction order.
Do not confuse optimization with permission to change defined behavior.
Do not confuse binary identity with behavioral equivalence.
Do not confuse behavioral equivalence with byte identity.
Do not confuse version numbers with exact artifact identity.
