Hash table iteration order should not be assumed unless explicitly guaranteed.
Changing implementation, runtime version, or insertion history can affect unspecified iteration order.
A tree is a hierarchical data structure.
A tree contains nodes.
A tree contains edges connecting nodes.
A parent is a node directly above another connected node according to the rooted relationship.
A node's depth describes its distance from the root according to edge count.
Tree height describes the maximum path depth according to the chosen definition.
