Health checks should test what they claim to test.
Liveness determines whether a component is sufficiently alive according to the liveness definition.
Liveness and readiness are different.
A process can be temporarily not ready while recovering.
Restarting a merely unready process can make recovery worse.
Health checks should not create failure loops.
A watchdog should monitor meaningful progress.
A process consuming CPU is not necessarily making progress.
Watchdog criteria should correspond to required operation.
A watchdog can restart a failed process.
Restart is not always the correct recovery.
