Failure should not be hidden indefinitely by automation.
Automation should reduce routine recovery work while preserving evidence.
Recovery actions should be logged.
Recovery outcomes should be recorded.
Observability supports reliability.
Logs record events.
Traces record operation paths.
Audit records preserve defined historical actions.
Alerts notify about conditions requiring awareness or action.
