Shared dependencies create common-mode risk.
Shared configuration can create common-mode risk.
Shared credentials can create common-mode risk.
Shared software defects can create common-mode risk.
Shared network infrastructure can create common-mode risk.
Shared storage can create common-mode risk.
Redundancy should be evaluated against actual failure modes.
