Manual failover provides human control.
Manual failover can increase outage duration.
Failure detection is imperfect in distributed systems.
A silent participant can be slow.
A silent participant can be partitioned.
A silent participant can be unreachable only from one observer.
Timeout-based failure detection produces suspicion.
Suspicion is not absolute proof.
Architecture should account for uncertain failure.
Split-brain can cause conflicting writes.
Authority must remain deterministic.
A stale component should not retain authority merely because it has not yet learned that authority changed.
