Escalate according to system policy when required.
When handling sensitive memory, minimize lifetime.
Minimize copies.
Prevent unnecessary logging.
Prevent unnecessary dumps.
Use appropriate memory protections where required.
Understand that complete erasure can require controls beyond one buffer overwrite.
When crossing module or library boundaries, define allocator ownership.
Prefer interfaces where allocation and release remain paired.
