The correct rule comes from system requirements.
Timestamps alone do not establish authority.
Version numbers alone do not establish authority.
Frequency of occurrence does not establish authority.
Algorithmic selection should encode actual governance rules.
A majority means more than half of the applicable voting set according to its definition.
A supermajority requires a threshold greater than ordinary majority according to the governing rule.
Quorum defines the participation required for a decision according to governance rules.
Do not substitute one voting rule for another.
Algorithms implement policy.
They do not create policy.
The human-defined governing rule determines the algorithm.
An algorithm should faithfully implement the authorized rule.
A policy change can require an algorithm change.
An algorithm should not silently reinterpret policy because another rule appears more efficient.
Execution authority and policy authority are different.
Algorithms do not acquire authority merely because they can execute them.
A recommendation algorithm selects or ranks options.
A recommendation is not a command.
A recommendation algorithm can use evidence.
A human can reject the recommendation.
Automation should remain within its delegated scope.
An algorithm operating outside its defined authority is an architectural defect even if its computation is technically correct.
A decision procedure should identify conditions under which it cannot decide.
Unknown can be a valid result.
Insufficient evidence can be a valid result.
Conflict can be a valid result.
Unsupported input can be a valid result.
Algorithms should not fabricate certainty to avoid returning unknown.
A three-state result can distinguish yes, no, and unknown.
A richer result can distinguish success, rejection, unavailable, malformed, unauthorized, and internal failure.
Return structures should preserve meaningful information.
Error codes are part of algorithm interfaces.
An error code should identify a defined failure category.
Zero is commonly used for success in C command-line and API conventions, but exact API contracts vary.
Positive values can represent errors in others.
