The correct policy depends on system requirements.
Access-control algorithms should evaluate identity.
Access-control algorithms should evaluate required authority.
Access-control algorithms can evaluate resource.
Access-control algorithms can evaluate action.
Access-control algorithms can evaluate contextual restrictions.
A successful authentication does not imply authorization.
