Preserving operator tokens and improving direct-evidence ranking solves a broader technical retrieval problem.
General repairs are preferable when evidence establishes a general defect.
Generalization should remain bounded.
Do not rewrite the entire retrieval architecture because one query failed.
Identify the underlying mechanism first.
Algorithms should be small enough to reason about.
A function performing one coherent transformation is easier to test.
