Algorithms should avoid hidden policy.
If retry count is policy, expose it appropriately.
If maximum lesson size is policy, expose it appropriately.
If ABI compatibility is policy, encode it explicitly.
Policy determines permitted behavior.
Algorithms implement behavior.
Data structures preserve required state.
Interfaces connect components.
Tests provide evidence.
Debugging identifies causes when behavior diverges.
These disciplines reinforce one another.
An algorithm should terminate when termination is required.
An infinite loop can be intentional for a service event loop.
