HttpOnly prevents ordinary client-side script access according to browser behavior.
SameSite can restrict selected cross-site cookie behavior.
These attributes address different risks.
Do not treat any one cookie attribute as complete session security.
Session cookies should not be transmitted over plaintext HTTP when secure transport is required.
Enforce HTTPS according to application policy.
Do not expose the same authenticated session over both protected and unprotected transport without an explicit design.
