Timestamp.
Source information where appropriate.
Authentication mechanism.
Credential changes.
Recovery operations.
Security-sensitive changes.
Do not log submitted passwords.
Do not log full reusable authentication tokens.
They can indicate automated guessing.
They can indicate credential stuffing.
They can indicate attack activity.
Rate limiting can reduce automated authentication abuse.
Rate limiting should be designed carefully.
