An attacker can intentionally lock other users out.
Consider multiple signals according to requirements.
Do not implement permanent account lockout after a small number of failures without considering abuse.
Backoff can slow repeated attempts.
Rate limits can apply to source addresses.
Rate limits can apply to accounts.
Rate limits can apply to device or session context.
Attackers can distribute requests.
Use evidence appropriate to the system.
