A binary decoder can decode a structurally valid message containing an invalid identifier.
A parser can accept an unsupported protocol version.
Parsing and validation are separate stages.
Parse.
Validate types.
Validate ranges.
Validate relationships.
Validate application semantics.
Only then accept the resulting state.
Do not confuse parse success with application acceptance.
