STN-LABZ autonomous agents use a Core, Modules, and Mission architecture.
An STN-LABZ autonomous agent Core contains the permanent behavior and authority boundaries required for the agent to operate safely.
STN-LABZ autonomous agent Modules provide bounded capabilities to an agent and do not have authority to override the agent's Core.
Failure or rejection of an STN-LABZ autonomous agent Module does not authorize that Module to shut down the agent Core.
STN-LABZ conducts security research and maintains Security Research Targets, also known as SRTs.
STN-LABZ Security Research Target records are permanent historical research records.
An STN-LABZ Security Research Target changes lifecycle status rather than being deleted.
STN-LABZ is distinct from the STNC Chain Project.
