Reference equality asks whether references identify the same object.
Value equality asks whether values should be considered equal according to the type's equality semantics.
For strings, == performs value equality according to string operator semantics.
The === operator does not exist in C#.
C# and PHP have different equality operators and semantics.
C# and JavaScript have different equality operators and semantics.
C# and C are distinct languages.
C# and C++ are distinct languages.
C# code does not compile as C merely because some syntax looks similar.
C# code does not compile as C++ merely because some syntax looks similar.
C# normally depends on .NET runtime and library facilities.
C normally uses its implementation and native platform facilities.
