Authentication, authorization, and signing remain separate.
Branches can be protected on hosting platforms.
Branch protection is a hosting-platform feature rather than a fundamental Git object property.
Protected branches can restrict direct pushes.
Protection rules support workflow policy.
Technical controls implement governance but do not define governance by themselves.
A pull request proposes integrating changes according to hosting workflow.
A pull request is not itself a Git commit.
A pull request can change as commits are added.
Approval of a pull request is a workflow event.
