The compiler can perform optimization.
Optimization attempts to improve generated code while preserving required observable program behavior according to language rules.
Optimization can reduce execution time.
Optimization can reduce code size.
Optimization can eliminate unnecessary calculations.
Optimization can rearrange operations where language semantics permit.
Optimization levels control optimization strategy according to the compiler.
GCC and Clang commonly provide options such as -O0, -O1, -O2, and -O3.
