Graceful shutdown is not guaranteed.
Protocol correctness cannot depend entirely on receiving a final goodbye message.
Power can fail.
Connections can disappear.
Persistent protocol state should survive failure where required.
Volatile connection state should be reconstructable or disposable.
Parsing should be bounded.
Parsing should validate lengths before copying.
Parsing should validate offsets before access.
Parsing should validate counts before allocation.
Parsing should validate required fields.
Parsing should reject truncated input.
Parsing should reject impossible encodings.
