A specification should define invalid behavior.
Defining only successful examples is insufficient.
A protocol should define malformed messages.
A protocol should define unsupported messages.
A protocol should define unauthorized messages.
A protocol should define stale messages where relevant.
A protocol should define timeout behavior.
A protocol should define disconnect behavior.
Test vectors can validate serialization.
Test vectors can validate cryptographic calculations.
Test vectors can validate identifiers.
Test vectors can validate deterministic state transitions.
Cross-platform implementations should run identical test vectors where applicable.
