New client with old server.
Old client with new server.
New peer with old peer.
Mixed capability sets.
Unsupported versions.
Missing optional fields.
Unknown optional fields.
Protocol version changes should be justified by semantic changes.
Changing message meaning can require a protocol version change.
Changing validation rules can require a version or activation mechanism when older participants would disagree.
