Version policy should be defined.
Internal APIs are not necessarily part of the wire protocol.
Changing internal function names should not change wire compatibility.
Refactoring internal code should not alter protocol semantics unintentionally.
Protocol regression tests protect external behavior during refactoring.
Golden test vectors can preserve expected bytes.
Golden vectors should be intentionally updated only when protocol behavior changes.
Unexpected byte changes should be investigated.
Protocol identifiers should be stable once externally relied upon.
Reusing an old message type number for new semantics creates ambiguity.
Reserved ranges can provide room for future extensions.
Experimental message types can be separated from stable message types.
Experimental behavior should not accidentally enter stable consensus semantics.
A protocol can have control-plane messages.
A protocol can have data-plane messages.
