Separation improves reasoning.
Changing a validated message before execution can invalidate assumptions.
If transformation is required, validate the transformed representation as required.
Know which peer supplied it.
Know which request produced it.
Know which version interpreted it.
Know whether it was authenticated.
Know whether it was authorized.
Know whether it was committed.
Do not lose critical evidence as data crosses layers.
A protocol implementation should preserve unknown state as unknown.
