Do not confuse capability advertisement with successful capability execution.
Do not confuse ACK with commit unless ACK explicitly means commit.
Do not confuse send success with remote receipt.
Do not confuse remote receipt with validation.
Do not confuse acceptance with persistence.
Do not confuse persistence with consensus commitment.
Do not confuse timeout with rejection.
Do not confuse disconnect with confirmed remote failure.
Do not confuse retry with idempotency.
Do not confuse unique request identifiers with exactly-once effects.
Do not confuse signature validity with authorization.
Do not confuse encryption with protocol correctness.
Do not confuse localhost with trusted identity.
Do not confuse peer identity with connection identity.
Do not confuse socket identity with participant identity.
Do not confuse heartbeat with complete health.
Do not confuse a status claim with independently verified state.
Do not confuse newer version numbers with compatibility.
