Define roles.
Define message types.
Define fields.
Define encoding.
Define limits.
Define versions.
Define capabilities.
Define states.
Define invalid transitions.
Define request correlation.
Define ordering.
Define duplicate behavior.
Define timeout behavior.
Define retry behavior.
Define authentication.
Define authorization.
Define shutdown.
Define restart behavior.
Define compatibility.
Define security boundaries.
Then implement.
When receiving a message, establish frame validity.
Establish protocol version.
Establish current state.
Establish message validity for that state.
Establish identity where required.
Establish freshness where required.
Establish authorization where required.
Establish semantic validity.
Only then perform authoritative effects.
When sending a message, use the negotiated protocol.
Use canonical encoding where required.
Use correct request identifiers.
Preserve required authentication.
Preserve required ordering.
Record enough state to interpret the response.
Do not send protocol messages that the current state forbids.
