Reliable automation should be deterministic where practical.
Given the same defined state and same defined event, the recovery decision should follow defined policy.
Hidden heuristics can make recovery difficult to audit.
Probabilistic guesses should not replace required evidence.
If authority is uncertain, do not invent authority.
If recovery cannot safely continue, escalate according to policy.
