Storage behavior is platform dependent.
Operating systems differ.
Storage devices differ.
Network filesystems differ.
Cloud storage systems differ.
Database engines differ.
Portable storage code should depend only on guarantees common to supported platforms or isolate platform-specific behavior behind defined interfaces.
A filesystem organizes persistent data as files, directories, metadata, and other filesystem-defined structures.
A file is a named or referenced sequence of data according to filesystem semantics.
A directory organizes filesystem entries.
