Quarantine can preserve corrupted or suspicious data outside active use.
Quarantine preserves evidence.
Quarantine can allow later analysis.
Quarantine storage should have controlled permissions.
Quarantine should have retention policy.
Do not automatically delete evidence unless policy permits it.
Disk space is finite.
Database capacity is finite.
Filesystem inode or metadata capacity can be finite.
Plan for limits.
Set bounds.
A storage-full condition should be expected.
Writes can fail when storage is full.
Logs can consume storage.
Temporary files can consume storage.
Caches can consume storage.
Application data can consume storage.
One class should not unexpectedly starve all others.
Separate quotas or volumes can provide isolation where appropriate.
