Headroom improves recoverability.
Storage growth should be observable.
Measure total capacity.
Measure used capacity.
Measure free capacity.
Measure growth rate.
Measure write rate.
Measure object count where relevant.
Measure database size.
Measure log size.
Forecasts are estimates.
Caches can evict according to policy.
Historical authoritative records may have permanent retention requirements.
Do not apply generic cleanup to permanent records.
Deletion has semantics.
Physical deletion removes stored representation according to storage behavior.
Archival moves data to another retention tier.
Tombstones record deletion state in selected distributed systems.
These are different operations.
A deleted file can remain recoverable from backups.
Deletion does not necessarily mean immediate physical erasure.
Secure erasure has stronger requirements.
Storage media can remap sectors.
Solid-state devices can complicate physical overwrite assumptions.
Do not promise irreversible physical deletion without understanding storage technology.
Historical systems can intentionally prohibit deletion.
