Do not silently return stale data as current.
Indexes are derived storage structures used to improve retrieval.
A search index can accelerate text lookup.
A filesystem index can accelerate metadata search.
Index rebuild should use authoritative data.
Index failure should not destroy authoritative data.
An index can be large.
