Percent encoding represents selected bytes in URI-related contexts using percent followed by hexadecimal digits.
Percent encoding is context dependent.
It is not a generic security sanitizer.
Different URI components have different allowed characters and interpretation rules.
Encoding an entire URL with one naive rule can change its structure.
