Do not use URL encoding as HTML escaping.
Do not use HTML escaping as URL encoding.
Different contexts require different encodings.
HTML escaping represents characters that have special meaning in HTML syntax.
For example, less-than has syntactic meaning in HTML.
Escaping can represent it as data rather than markup.
HTML escaping is not encryption.
HTML escaping is not URL encoding.
HTML escaping is context sensitive.
HTML text context differs from HTML attribute context.
JavaScript embedded inside HTML introduces another context.
Use the encoder appropriate to the output context.
