Security requires correct separation between commands and data.
Encoding can help representation.
It does not grant safety automatically.
JSON string escaping represents special characters within JSON strings.
Backslashes require escaping.
Control characters require defined representations.
A JSON serializer should perform JSON escaping.
Escaping and character encoding are different layers.
A JSON string can contain escaped Unicode notation.
The complete JSON document can then be encoded as UTF-8 bytes.
The escape syntax exists inside the JSON representation.
