Given the same sequence of Unicode code points and the same defined encoding, a conforming encoder should produce the same bytes.
If normalization is required, normalization rules must also be fixed.
If line-ending normalization is required, it must be fixed.
If escaping is required, escaping rules must be fixed.
Do not let platform locale change authoritative output.
Do not let host-native line endings change consensus-visible bytes.
Do not let serializer defaults choose an unspecified encoding.
Canonical bytes require explicit rules at every transformation layer.
An encoded value can be validated against a canonical representation.
Decode the value.
Re-encode according to canonical rules.
Compare if the protocol defines this method.
