Machine interfaces should prefer one canonical form.
Whitespace can be significant.
Whitespace can be insignificant.
The grammar determines which.
Do not trim arbitrary encoded values.
A Base64 protocol can permit or forbid whitespace.
A token can legitimately contain leading or trailing characters that appear like whitespace under another interpretation.
Trimming is a transformation.
Only perform it when specified.
